## Plotly Library
We provide direct bindings to API of Plotly.js. Try out some the of basic charts

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Plotly Library
We provide direct bindings to API of Plotly.js. Try out some the of basic charts

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
data = Table[{x, Sinc[6x]}, {x,0, 2Pi, 0.1}];

plot = Plotly[<|
  "x"->data[[All,1]],
  "y"->data[[All,2]],
  "mode"->"lines"
|>]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(PlotlyInstance[FrontEndRef["F8beeb8b4-b335-4816-84ab-25d4421292cf"],WindowObj[<|"Socket" -> USocketObject[7]|>]])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgUJWySlpiZZJJnoJhkbm+qaWBia6VqYJCbpGpmmmJgYGRpZGiWnAQCdvhW5"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Now `plot` acts like an instance of the visible plot. To add more traces simply evaluate:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Now `plot` acts like an instance of the visible plot. To add more traces simply evaluate:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
PlotlyAddTraces[plot, {
  <|"x"->data[[All,1]], "y"->Reverse[data[[All,2]]]|>
}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Missing["NotConnected"]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Plotly automatically rescales and adds legends. This can be done with almost any plot type.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Plotly automatically rescales and adds legends. This can be done with almost any plot type.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
### Other charts
Pie, bars, bubble chart. Plotly has almost everything!

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
### Other charts
Pie, bars, bubble chart. Plotly has almost everything!

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
trace = <| 
	"values" -> {19, 26, 55}, 
	"labels" -> {"Residential", "Non-Residential", "Utility"}, 
	"type" -> "pie" 
|>;

Plotly[trace]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(PlotlyInstance[FrontEndRef["Ffee7f622-4b0e-4e41-8a96-823ca162820b"],WindowObj[<|"Socket" -> USocketObject[7]|>]])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgUJp6WmmqeZGRnpmiQZpOqapJoY6lokWprpWhgZJycamhlZGBkkAQCfzRW4"*)(*]VB*)

